Atlas","/farmland-atlas/arkansas/scott-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record here runs 75 years, 1951 to 2025, and on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 12 grids November to December came in under 90% of normal in 37 of them. In 2025 that same pair hit 46% of normal on the middle, while April to May ran 151%. In 2026 so far, January to February sat at 50% on the middle. Every grid&rsquo;s driest year was 1963, and grid 17843 got just 49% of normal that year.</p>"}
